import json,hashlib
from pathlib import Path
D=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
suffix='\nGive a complete, concise mathematical justification. Do not assume the conclusion. Any correct method is allowed. Clearly state your final result.'
rows=[
('F01','single_similarity','A point S outside a circle has a tangent ST. A secant meets the circle at U,V in the order S,U,V, with SU=3 and UV=9. Find ST. Establish the product identity you use from similar triangles instead of citing the power-of-a-point theorem.','ST=6. Triangles STU and SVT are similar: S corresponds to S, T to V, U to T. ST/SV=SU/ST.'),
('F02','single_cyclic_similarity','Two chords AC and BD of a circle meet at an interior point P. PA=3, PC=8, PB=4. Find PD. Derive the needed product relation from angles and similar triangles instead of quoting the intersecting-chords theorem.','PD=6. Triangles APB and DPC: angle APB=DPC vertical; angle PAB=PDC subtend CB. PA/PD=PB/PC.'),
('F03','composition_right_altitude','Triangle ABC is right-angled at A. The perpendicular from A to BC meets BC at D. Given BD=4 and DC=9, find AD and AB. Justify the relations rather than citing a special theorem about the altitude to a hypotenuse.','AD=6; AB=2sqrt(13). Triangles ABD and CAD are similar giving AD²=BD*DC. ABC similar DBA gives AB²=BD*BC=52.'),
('F04','composition_hidden_circle','ABC is an acute triangle. D is the foot of the perpendicular from B to AC, and E is the foot from C to AB. Prove that angle ADE equals angle ABC.','B,C,D,E lie on the circle with diameter BC. For their order, angle CDE+angle CBE=180 degrees; angle ADE=180-angle CDE=angle ABC.'),
('F05','composition_parallel_lengths','ABCD is a convex trapezoid with AB parallel to CD, AB=6, CD=10. Diagonals AC and BD intersect at O. The line through O parallel to the bases meets AD at E and BC at F. Find EF.','EF=15/2. Similar AOB,COD give AO/OC=3/5. AEO similar ADC gives EO=10*(3/8)=15/4; CFO similar CBA gives OF=6*(5/8)=15/4.'),
('F06','composition_converse_parallel','In triangle ABC, D is inside AB and E is inside AC, with AD/DB=AE/EC=2/3. Lines BE and CD intersect at F. Find BF/FE.','BF/FE=5/2. AD/AB=AE/AC=2/5, hence DE parallel BC and DE/BC=2/5. BFC and EFD are similar.'),
('F07','composition_tangent_lengths','The two tangents from T touch a circle at A and B, and TA=7. A third tangent touches the minor arc AB at P and meets the segments TA and TB at X and Y. Assume P lies between X and Y, with T,X,A and T,Y,B in those respective orders. Find the perimeter of triangle TXY.','Perimeter=14. XA=XP and YB=YP; TA=TB=7. TX+TY+XY=TX+TY+XA+YB=TA+TB.'),
('F08','composition_tangent_parallel','A,B,C are distinct points on a circle. The line through C parallel to the tangent at A meets the ray AB at D, with A,B,D in that order. Prove AB*AD=AC^2.','Triangles ABC and ACD are similar by the common A angle and tangent-chord theorem with CD parallel tangent. AB/AC=AC/AD.'),
('F09','composition_area_auxiliary','ABC is an isosceles triangle with AB=AC. P is any point in the interior of BC. E and F are the perpendicular projections of P onto the lines AB and AC. Prove that PE+PF equals the perpendicular distance from B to line AC.','Introduce AP. Area ABC=area ABP+area ACP=(AB*PE+AC*PF)/2=AC*(PE+PF)/2. Also area ABC=AC*h_B/2.'),
('F10','composition_trapezoid_auxiliary','ABCD is a convex trapezoid with AB parallel to CD, AB>CD, and AD=BC. Prove that A,B,C,D lie on one circle.','For instance drop perpendiculars from D,C to AB, or intersect extended legs at P. Similar PDC,PAB and equal AD,BC imply PD=PC, hence equal base angles; parallel bases give opposite angles supplementary. Exclude the parallelogram case using AB>CD.'),
('F11','invalid_cyclic_side_condition','Four distinct points A,B,C,D have no three collinear. Suppose angle BAC equals angle BDC, where both angles are ordinary angles in (0,180 degrees). Must the four points lie on one circle? Prove the assertion or give an explicit counterexample.','No. B=(-1,0), C=(1,0), A=(0,2), D=(0,-2) yield equal reflected angles but are not concyclic. Circle ABC has center (0,3/4), radius5/4, excluding D. Equal ordinary subtended angles need the correct side condition.'),
('F12','invalid_ssa_correspondence','Two nondegenerate triangles ABC and DEF satisfy AB/DE=AC/DF and angle ABC=angle DEF. Must the triangles be similar with correspondence A-D, B-E, C-F? Prove it or give an explicit counterexample.','No, SSA. Set B=E=(0,0), A=D=(sqrt(3),1), C=(sqrt(3)+1,0), F=(sqrt(3)-1,0). AB=DE=2, AC=DF=sqrt(2), B=E=30 degrees, yet BC differs from EF.'),
]
jobs=[dict(id=i,skill=skill,problem=p+suffix,reference=ref,stratum='foundation_dev',training_eligible=False) for i,skill,p,ref in rows]
(D/'screen-jobs.json').write_text(json.dumps(jobs,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
models={}
base=json.loads(Path('qwen/models.json').read_text())['models']['qwen3_4b']
models['qwen3_4b']=dict(model_id=base['model_id'],revision=base['revision'],snapshot=base['snapshot_path'],status='complete')
for key,old in [('qwen3_2507','qwen3_2507_en'),('qwen35_9b','qwen35_9b')]:
 models[key]=json.loads((D.parent/'model-search-2026-09-23'/f'{old}-model.json').read_text())
for key,meta in models.items():(D/f'{key}-model.json').write_text(json.dumps(meta,indent=2)+'\n')
protocol=dict(phase='foundation_screen',models=['qwen3_4b','qwen3_2507','qwen35_9b','r1_8b'],samples_per_problem=2,max_output_tokens=8192,max_context=12288,dtype='bfloat16',kv_cache_dtype='auto',tool_access=False,language='en',seed=2026092319,model_watchdog_seconds=2700,total_screen_answers=96,updates=0,
 sampling={'qwen3_4b':dict(temperature=.6,top_p=.95,top_k=20),'qwen3_2507':dict(temperature=.6,top_p=.95,top_k=20),'qwen35_9b':dict(temperature=1.,top_p=.95,top_k=20,presence_penalty=1.5),'r1_8b':dict(temperature=.6,top_p=.95,top_k=-1)},
 decisions=['Use completed valid reasoning, spontaneous geometric use, truncation and cost separately.','This is a model-plus-recommended-setting comparison, not an architecture causal test.','Screen is development data; do not train on these questions or choose checkpoint on the target proof evaluation.','If one candidate already solves simple unseen compositions reliably, foundation FT is not a prerequisite.','Before SFT, freeze independent confirmation questions and target-development checks.','At most one small foundation SFT recipe initially; online target RL is outside this pilot.'],
 jobs_sha256=hashlib.sha256((D/'screen-jobs.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest())
(D/'protocol.json').write_text(json.dumps(protocol,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
print(json.dumps({'problems':len(jobs),'models':protocol['models'],'jobs_sha256':protocol['jobs_sha256']}))
